From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:09:04 +0900
Subject: Android host: the desktop session survives the host going away

When the Android host (the Rungic app) was closed, killed (a vendor's battery manager, low memory),
updated or restarted, KWin exited with 133 for kwin_wayland_wrapper to restart it, and the app then
restarted the whole desktop session: every window and anything unsaved was lost, though the Linux
container and its processes were alive.

Now the lost connection is reported once and never read again (WaylandDisplay); the backend drops
the phone's and cast outputs (the workspace keeps the windows on its placeholder output), the input
devices and the buffers imported on the connection (WaylandBackend::disconnectHost), and keeps the
dead display allocated, as proxies of it may still be released. Every 500 ms it checks whether the
host's socket answers, then connects again (connectHost, without the initial 60 s wait): new outputs
and seat, the host's globals, text input and idle inhibition. The windows return to the phone's
output.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-05
X-Rungic-Status: Pending
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:session.ready
